Eleven register examples include uvm_pkg.sv, the file that defines the UVM
package, instead of importing the package the UVM library defines. A package
is defined once across every compilation unit (IEEE 1800-2023 3.13 b), so
wherever UVM is compiled as a library of its own, as its README directs, the
include defines uvm_pkg a second time. Include only the UVM macros, as the
README directs and as the other examples do. Each file already imports
uvm_pkg, so what it reads is unchanged.

Not sent to the suite, since UVM 1.2 is a closed Accellera release.

diff --git a/examples/simple/registers/models/aliasing/tb_run.sv b/examples/simple/registers/models/aliasing/tb_run.sv
--- a/examples/simple/registers/models/aliasing/tb_run.sv
+++ b/examples/simple/registers/models/aliasing/tb_run.sv
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 // -------------------------------------------------------------
 // 
 
-`include "uvm_pkg.sv"
+`include "uvm_macros.svh"
 
 program tb;
 
